  "necessity_paragraph": "The patient presents with recurrent episodes of palpitations and lightheadedness consistent with supraventricular tachycardia, occurring against a background of known atherosclerotic heart disease of the native coronary artery (I47.1, I25.10). Mobile cardiac telemetry (CPT 93229) is ordered to capture intermittent arrhythmic events and correlate symptoms with rhythm disturbances in an outpatient setting. The payer denied the claim under CO-197 for missing precertification, but the service was medically necessary to document the documented history of supraventricular tachycardia and coronary artery disease."
